</ext-link>. Accessed 17 July 2007</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040256-b026"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group><name><surname>Farber</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>1992</year><article-title>Fatal distraction</article-title><comment>Spin Magazine. Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.virusmyth.net/aids/data/cffatal.htm">http://www.virusmyth.net/aids/data/cffatal.htm</ext-link>. Accessed 17 July 2007</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040256-b027"><citation citation-type="other"><collab>&#x0005b;No authors listed&#x0005d;</collab><year>2006</year><article-title>Harpers astonishes the world with the extent of AIDS skulduggery</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.paradigmoverthrow.com/blog/harpers-astonishes-the-world-with-the-extent-of-aids-skulduggery.htm">http://www.paradigmoverthrow.com/blog/harpers-astonishes-the-world-with-the-extent-of-aids-skulduggery.htm</ext-link>. Accessed 17 July 2007</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040256-b028"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Duesberg</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><year>1989</year><article-title>Human immunodeficiency virus and acquired immunodeficiency syndrome: Correlation but not causation</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>86</volume><fpage>755</fpage><lpage>764</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2644642</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040256-b029"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Holtgrave</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Causes of the decline in AIDS deaths, United States, 1995&#x02013;2002: prevention, treatment or both?</article-title><source>Int J STD AIDS</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>777</fpage><lpage>781</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16336756</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040256-b030"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group><name><surname>Harrison-Chirimuuta</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Is AIDS African?</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.virusmyth.net/aids/data/rcdisson.htm">http://www.virusmyth.net/aids/data/rcdisson.htm</ext-link>. Accessed 17 July 2007</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040256-b031"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Duesberg</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><year>1992</year><article-title>AIDS acquired by drug consumption and other noncontagious risk factors</article-title><source>Pharmacol Ther</source><volume>55</volume><fpage>201</fpage><lpage>277</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1492119</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040256-b032"><citation citation-type="journal"><collab>&#x0005b;No authors listed&#x0005d;</collab><year>2006</year><article-title>Denying science</article-title><source>Nat Med</source><volume>12</volume><fpage>369</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16598265</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040256-b033"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Bogart</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Thorburn</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Are HIV/AIDS conspiracy beliefs a barrier to HIV prevention among African Americans?</article-title><source>J Acquir Immune Defic Syndr</source><volume>38</volume><fpage>213</fpage><lpage>218</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15671808</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040256-b034"><citation citation-type="other"><collab>National Science Board</collab><year>2004</year><article-title>Science and technology: Public attitudes and understanding</article-title><comment>Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.nsf.gov/statistics/seind04/c7/c7s2.htm">